  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Audit: Evidence Manifest and Receipt Chain Design",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Status: Draft Date: 2026-05-13 Branch: main HEAD: e389b446706173ebc5950931994ba4cdb6a7d9f4 Scope: Read-only design audit Owner area: evidence",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Executive Summary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This document designs a verifiable evidence graph for Rig Relay. Currently, evidence files (observability logs, artifacts, context reports) exist in the filesystem but are not cryptographically linked. We propose a `manifest.json` that acts as the anchor for a session's integrity, enabling detection of corruption, deletion, or tampering.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Current implemented state: - a minimal per-session `manifest.json` already exists - `rig-relay doctor evidence` validates one selected session read-only - the validator prefers the manifest when present and falls back to scan-based validation for legacy sessions - the next layer remains receipt-chain / Merkle work, not root-default policy changes",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Proposed Docs Path",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "`docs/architecture/evidence-manifest-receipt-chain.md`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Evidence Manifest Schema Sketch",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-9",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "json",
      "content": "{\n  \"schema_version\": \"rig.relay.manifest.v1\",\n  \"session_id\": \"uuid-or-hash\",\n  \"root_mode\": \"repo_local\",\n  \"created_at\": \"ISO-8601\",\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"file_path\": \"observability.jsonl\",\n      \"event_range\": [0, 10],\n      \"sha256\": \"file-level-hash\",\n      \"line_hashes\": [\"hash1\", \"hash2\", \"...\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file_path\": \"context/assembly_abc123.json\",\n      \"event_id\": \"event-uuid-1\",\n      \"sha256\": \"hash\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"final_hash\": \"merkle-root-of-all-entries\"\n}",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "detailed",
        "collapsible": true,
        "collapsed_by_default": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Receipt Chain Options",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1.  **Append-Only Journal**: The manifest is a `.jsonl` itself, where each new evidence file added to the session appends a \"receipt\" line. This is robust against mid-session crashes. 2.  **Session Finalizer**: A single `manifest.json` written when the session closes. Simpler but loses evidence if the agent is killed. 3.  **Merkle-Linked Observability**: Each event in `observability.jsonl` contains the hash of the previous event, creating a blockchain-like chain of custody.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Recommended Minimal Implementation Slice (Slice 4)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Implement a `ManifestManager` that tracks all files written during a session. - Write a `manifest.jsonl` in the session directory. - Add `manifest_sha256` to the `SESSION_CLOSED` event.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Risks and Non-Goals",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **Non-Goal**: We are not implementing a global ledger or blockchain. The proof is local to the repository. - **Risk**: Performance overhead of hashing large artifacts on every turn. - **Risk**: Clock skew affecting `created_at` ordering if multiple processes write to the same root (mitigated by sequence numbers).",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Migration/Backward-Compatibility Plan",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Old sessions without manifests will be treated as \"Unverifiable\". - `DuckDBProjection` will warn but still process sessions missing manifests.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Tests Required Before Implementation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `test_manifest_detects_deleted_artifact` - `test_manifest_detects_corrupt_jsonl_line` - `test_manifest_handles_mid_session_crash`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
